@startuml sequence_diagram_google_login_failure
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - AA02 Cancelled or Failed Google Sign-In

actor User as "Client / User"
participant SPA as "SPA (Front-End)\nGoogleCallbackPage"
participant Google as "Google Identity Services\n(OIDC Provider)"
participant Routes as "AuthRoutes"
participant Validator as "ValidationMiddleware\n(Joi)"
participant Controller as "AuthController"
participant ExtService as "ExternalAuthenticationService"
participant Store as "IAuthorizationStateStore\n(InMemory)"
participant IdP as "IExternalIdentityProvider\n(GoogleOidcProvider)"

note over User, Google
    Precondition: phase 1 of SD 1 was completed:
    a pending { state, nonce, codeVerifier } exists in the store,
    the SPA saved "oidc_state" and the browser is at Google.
    This diagram shows failure branches only; each one ends
    the interaction without issuing a LaPrizza token.
end note

activate Google
Google -> User : Google sign-in and consent screen

alt 1) User cancels or denies consent at Google
    User -> Google : cancel / deny
    Google --> SPA : 302 redirect_uri?error=access_denied&state=...
    deactivate Google
    activate SPA
    SPA -> SPA : remove stored "oidc_state";\nno call to the back end
    SPA --> User : "Google sign-in was cancelled.\nYou have not been signed in."\n(stays on login page as Guest)
    deactivate SPA
    note right of Store
        The unused pending entry
        expires after its TTL (10 min).
    end note

else User authenticates at Google
    User -> Google : Google credentials + consent
    Google --> SPA : 302 redirect_uri?code=...&state=...
    deactivate Google
    activate SPA
    SPA -> SPA : compare query state with\nsessionStorage "oidc_state"

    alt 2) Returned state does not match the state stored in this browser
        SPA -> SPA : remove stored "oidc_state";\nno call to the back end\n(possible login CSRF / stale tab)
        SPA --> User : "Sign-in could not be completed.\nPlease try again."

    else State matches: send code to the back end
        SPA -> SPA : remove stored "oidc_state"
        SPA -> Routes : POST /api/v1/auth/google/callback\n{ code, state }
        activate Routes
        Routes -> Validator : ValidationMiddleware.validate(schemas.googleCallback)\n(req, res, next)
        activate Validator

        alt 3) Invalid payload (missing / oversized code or state, unknown fields)
            Validator --> SPA : 400 Bad Request\n{ error: { message: "Invalid request body", status: 400 } }
            deactivate Validator
            SPA --> User : "Sign-in could not be completed.\nPlease try again."

        else Payload valid
            activate Validator
            Validator --> Routes : next()
            deactivate Validator
            Routes -> Controller : completeGoogleLogin(req, res)
            activate Controller
            Controller -> ExtService : completeAuthorization(new ExternalCallbackDTO(req.body))
            activate ExtService
            ExtService -> Store : consume(state)

            alt 4) Unknown, expired or already used state (replay)
                Store --> ExtService : null (no pending authorization)

            else State valid
                Store --> ExtService : pending { nonce, codeVerifier }\n(entry removed: single use)
                ExtService -> IdP : exchangeAndVerify(code, codeVerifier, nonce)
                activate IdP
                IdP -> Google : POST token endpoint\n(code, client_id, client_secret,\nredirect_uri, code_verifier)
                activate Google

                alt 5) Code rejected by Google or Google unreachable
                    Google --> IdP : invalid_grant error / no response
                    deactivate Google
                    IdP --> ExtService : throw code exchange failed

                else Tokens returned
                    activate Google
                    Google --> IdP : { id_token, access_token }
                    deactivate Google
                    IdP -> IdP : verify id_token: signature (Google JWKS),\niss, aud, exp, nonce; check email_verified

                    alt 6) ID token invalid (signature, iss, aud, exp or nonce)
                        IdP --> ExtService : throw invalid ID token
                    else 7) email_verified is false or e-mail missing
                        IdP --> ExtService : throw unverified e-mail
                    end
                end
                deactivate IdP
            end

            ExtService -> ExtService : log failure reason without code,\ntokens or secrets (AA05 audit-safe)
            ExtService --> Controller : throw AppError("External authentication failed", 401)
            deactivate ExtService
            Controller --> SPA : 401 Unauthorized\n{ error: { message: "External authentication failed", status: 401 } }
            deactivate Controller
            SPA --> User : "Google sign-in failed. Please try again\nor use local sign-in."\n(no token stored, protected pages unavailable)
        end
        deactivate Routes
    end
    deactivate SPA
end

note over User, IdP
    In every branch no AuthTokenDTO is issued, so no protected functionality becomes available (AC 6).
    The same uniform 401 message is used for all back-end authentication failures (4 to 7);
    the specific reason is kept only in server logs.
end note

@enduml